An opt-in `--decreases-literal-axiom-only` option leaves out a function's all-literals definition axiom when its `decreases` clause names only some of its parameters, so that a call whose arguments are all literals unfolds through one literal axiom instead of two.  With both, the cost of such a call grew about fourfold per level of a literal term (with Z3 5.1.0, 405,000 resource units at depth 4 and out of resources at depth 6, against 13,696 and 19,641 with the option).  Writing `decreases t` (or `decreases this` for a datatype member) is how a literal term unfolds when another argument is not a literal, as in https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/197 and https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/198; the Reference Manual's `{:fuel}` section now says so.
